## Advisory notes (non-blocking)

1. BOX-SIZING ON HOLLOW ELEMENTS: No global box-sizing: border-box reset.
   The hollow fasti tick (.fasti-strip__tick--hollow, border: 1px solid on a
   3px element) renders at 5x5px content-box vs 3x3px filled. Same issue on
   gate-ladder hollow marks (8x8 vs 6x6). Add box-sizing: border-box to
   .fasti-strip__tick and .gate-ladder__mark, or add a global reset. This
   is a visual alignment bug, not a logic or spec violation.

2. GATE LADDER bad-diagonal: The clip-path polygon(0 100%, 100% 0, 100% 100%)
   renders a triangle, not "bad fill with a 1px diagonal" as DIRECTION.md
   section 4.1 specifies. The accessibility requirement (shape difference
   surviving color blindness) IS met. The visual is a reasonable 6px-scale
   interpretation but does not literally match the spec's description of a
   filled mark with a diagonal line overlaid. Consider a pseudo-element or
   linear-gradient approach for the 1px diagonal on a fully filled bad mark.

3. CLOSED-DAY FASTI STATE: The builder correctly documented (ponytail comment
   in fasti.ts) that the frozen API has no per-day closed/open signal, so all
   non-landing days show hollow instead of the three-state behavior described
   in DIRECTION.md section 4.2. This is an API limitation, not a code defect.

4. NAV LINK COLOR: Nav links use var(--ink). DIRECTION.md section 3 says
   "Verdigris — links." Arguable whether nav items are "links" in this context
   vs content hyperlinks. Not blocking.
